{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/listener_closed_early_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":21,"end_line":12,"end_col":41,"message":"`l` is not used after this call, so a compiled program closes the listener here, before the next line runs: a connection to its port is refused. (The interpreter keeps it open, so the program behaves differently there.) Use `l` again where you are done with it, for example `Socket.close_listener(l)`.","code":"listener_closed_early","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"PROGRAM"}
